WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:04.300
The Spider-Man debacle between Sony and Marvel
is getting even stickier.

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:08.540
When it was reported at the end of August
2019 that the two studios had failed to reach

00:00:08.540 --> 00:00:12.530
an agreement to renegotiate terms of their
deal that allows Tom Holland's Spider-Man

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:14.700
to be a part of the Marvel Cinematic Universe
...

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:15.880
"Who would do something like that?"

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:20.140
… it seemed that the main reason why things
came crashing down was financial in nature.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.810
Disney, which owns Marvel Studios, was said
to have requested a 50 percent co-financing

00:00:24.810 --> 00:00:29.259
stake in the Spider-Man franchise - a dramatic
increase from its previous five percent yield

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:32.780
from day-one profits - which Sony reportedly
denied without countering.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:38.500
Now, Sony Pictures CEO and chairman Tony Vinciquerra
has revealed another reason for the Spider-Man

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:42.380
split with Marvel — and it doesn't have
anything to do with Disney and Marvel wanting

00:00:42.380 --> 00:00:42.960
more money.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:48.440
During Variety's Entertainment and Technology
summit on September 5th, 2019, Vinciquerra

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.820
stated that Marvel Studios president Kevin
Feige had been "stretched incredibly thin"

00:00:52.820 --> 00:00:56.940
following Disney's March 2019 acquisition
of 20th Century Fox.

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.850
With Feige's workload ramping up to include
discussions and plans for what to do with

00:01:00.850 --> 00:01:05.890
the X-Men, the Fantastic Four, Deadpool, and
more, the studio head apparently became overwhelmed

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:10.200
and evidently could no longer properly focus
on keeping Spidey in the MCU.

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.420
According to Variety, Vinciquerra pointed
to this as "one of the reasons behind the

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:18.680
breakdown" in conversations about establishing
new terms of the Spider-Man deal.

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:23.180
What certainly didn't cause the divorce was
bad blood, as Vinciquerra affirmed that there

00:01:23.189 --> 00:01:25.820
was and is "no ill will" between Sony and
Marvel.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:30.119
He also had some nice things to say about
working with Feige, who produced both Spider-Man:

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:34.729
Homecoming and Spider-Man: Far From Home,
and noted that neither Sony nor Marvel simply

00:01:34.729 --> 00:01:37.620
threw in the towel in regards to the Spider-Man
franchise, saying,

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:40.460
"We had a great run with [Feige] on Spider-Man
movies.

00:01:40.460 --> 00:01:42.340
We tried to see if there's a way to work it
out.

00:01:42.490 --> 00:01:46.340
The Marvel people are terrific people, we
have great respect for them, but on the other

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:48.560
hand we have some pretty terrific people of
our own.

00:01:48.760 --> 00:01:50.000
Kevin didn't do all the work."

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:55.380
Vinciquerra also made a sad confession about
the situation: there's no chance of reconciliation

00:01:55.380 --> 00:01:56.180
as of right now.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:00.240
He explained that, quote, "for the moment,
the door is closed" on having a professional

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:03.270
relationship with Marvel, and the studio is
"not for sale."

00:02:03.440 --> 00:02:07.619
Vinciquerra also detailed that Sony has big
plans for Spider-Man without the House of

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:08.320
Mouse involved.

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:13.040
A Spider-Man universe is well underway - set
to include the Tom Hardy-topped Venom and

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:18.069
the upcoming Venom sequel, the Morbius movie
starring Jared Leto, and "five or six" television

00:02:18.069 --> 00:02:20.379
series that take place within the Spider-Man
world.

00:02:20.379 --> 00:02:24.739
The executive reiterated that Spider-Man is
going to do "just fine" after swinging out

00:02:24.739 --> 00:02:29.720
of the MCU, using the Academy Award-winning
animated film Spider-Man: Into the Spider-Verse

00:02:29.720 --> 00:02:33.140
as an example of the famous hero thriving
without input from Marvel.

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:34.260
Vinciquerra said,

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:38.540
"Spider-Man was fine before the event movies,
did better with the event movies, and now

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:41.799
that we have our own universe, he will play
off the other characters as well.

00:02:41.799 --> 00:02:44.440
I think we're pretty capable of doing what
we have to do here."

00:02:44.440 --> 00:02:49.110
Clearly, Sony executives are confident that
Spider-Man will succeed without Feige, Marvel,

00:02:49.110 --> 00:02:52.140
and Disney - but what does Spidey himself
think about all this?

00:02:52.300 --> 00:02:56.600
Star Tom Holland has remained diplomatic about
the split and hasn't taken sides, stating

00:02:56.610 --> 00:03:00.709
that playing Spider-Man has been a dream come
true and that he knows the hero's franchise

00:03:00.709 --> 00:03:02.140
is in safe hands with Sony.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:02.820
"You ready?"

00:03:03.040 --> 00:03:03.540
"Yeah."

00:03:03.700 --> 00:03:04.640
"You're gonna love this."

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:11.230
What happens next for Spider-Man is slightly
unclear - at least in terms of where his story

00:03:11.230 --> 00:03:15.650
will head after Spider-Man: Far From Home,
which tied into several past MCU movies and

00:03:15.650 --> 00:03:20.200
included a number of MCU characters - but
we do know that Holland is lined up to appear

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:21.840
in at least two more movies at Sony.

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:25.800
As for Marvel, the studio is gearing up to
enter the fourth phase of the MCU.

00:03:25.800 --> 00:03:29.460
Meanwhile, Feige is getting his footing as
the new head of the X-Men film franchise,

00:03:29.500 --> 00:03:33.240
which he reportedly plans to reboot with a
brand-new, younger Wolverine.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:37.440
Here's hoping he can juggle it all and avoid
getting stretched too thin yet again.

